        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "A mixture of ethanol (1 mL) and acetonitrile (1 mL) was added to a Pyrex tube containing 2-methylpropane-1,3-diol (0.0105 g, 0.1 mmol), 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde (0.0172 g, 0.1 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.0568 g, 0.1 mmol), Ni(NO3)2·4H2O (0.0255 g, 0.1 mmol), and triethylamine (50 μL). The mixture was thoroughly mixed and sealed under vacuum. The resulting clear green solution was heated at 80 °C for 15 hours, then slowly cooled to ambient temperature under air. Light green crystals formed upon cooling were isolated by filtration, affording a yield of 38% based on Dy content. The Schiff-base ligand HL is generated in situ from 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde and 2-methylpropane-1,3-diol.",
