        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Cluster 1 is a zero-dc-field single-molecule magnet. Room-temperature χMT is 49.69 cm3 K mol−1 (slightly above the spin-only value 48.51 cm3 K mol−1 for three DyIII and six NiII) and falls to 7.83 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.0 K. Exchange fitting gives antiferromagnetic J1 (Ni···Ni) and weak antiferromagnetic J2 and J3 (Dy···Dy). Magnetization reaches 25.00 NμB at 2 K and 50 kOe without saturation, and hysteresis at 2 K shows no apparent coercivity. AC susceptibility (0–1000 Hz, 0 Oe) shows slow relaxation; Orbach, QTM, and Raman pathways give Ueff = 19.41 K.",
